#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186100521 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "41b7d83f-3b9b-556c-9e49-13df9c3b597e" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating Functions Containing the Natural Logarithm"}] :question/id #uuid "8ea17e06-1248-510c-9e71-c57da0cb0d02" :question/math-academy-id "e-14405" :question/problem "Calculate $\\displaystyle{\\int \\dfrac{3}{x \\sqrt{\\ln x}} \\, \\textrm{d}x }.$" :question/worked-solution "Let's set $u = \\ln x.$ Then, we have\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}u}{\\textrm{d}x}= \\dfrac 1 x\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad \\textrm{d}u=\\dfrac 1 x\\,{\\textrm{d}x}.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{3}{x\\sqrt{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}}\\,\\text{d}x & =3\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}}\\cdot \\frac{1}{x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =3\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{u}}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =3\\int {u}^{-1/2}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =3\\cdot 2{u}^{1/2}+C \\\\  & =6\\sqrt{u}+C \\\\  & =6\\sqrt{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}+C\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186100522 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "fa28f5c4-135e-576a-baa0-68c41b5139f6" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating Functions Containing Other Logarithms"}] :question/id #uuid "1579f932-6e7f-5daa-b001-54a9f6c236ad" :question/math-academy-id "e-14406" :question/problem "Calculate the integral $\\displaystyle \\int \\dfrac{\\log^2_3 x }{x} \\,\\textrm d x.$" :question/worked-solution "Let's rewrite our integral as\n\n$$\n\\int \\dfrac{(\\log_3 x)^2 }{x} \\,\\textrm d x.\n$$\n\nLet $u=\\log_3 x.$ Differentiating, we get\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm d u}{\\textrm d x} = \\dfrac{1}{x\\ln 3}\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad\\ln 3\\,\\textrm d u = \\dfrac 1 x \\textrm d x.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{({log}_{3}⁡x)^{2}}{x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int ({log}_{3}⁡x)^{2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int {u}^{2}\\cdot \\operatorname{ln}⁡3\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡3\\int {u}^{2}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡3\\cdot \\frac{1}{3}{u}^{3}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡3({log}_{3}⁡x)^{3}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡3{log}_{3}^{3}⁡x+C\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186100523 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "37a7aff6-d1b2-5383-bb26-aa6363594b05" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating Definite Integrals"}] :question/id #uuid "d2f49acf-ed91-510d-a0f1-41c50eeef9e7" :question/math-academy-id "e-14422" :question/problem "Evaluate $\\displaystyle{\\int_{e}^{e^2} \\dfrac{\\ln^2 x}{x}\\,\\textrm{d}x}.$" :question/worked-solution "Let's set $u = \\ln x.$ Then, we have\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}u}{\\textrm{d}x}= \\dfrac 1 x\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad \\textrm{d}u=\\dfrac 1 x\\,{\\textrm{d}x}.\n$$\n\nCalculating the limits for $u$ gives the following:\n\n| $x$ | $e$ | $e^2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $1$ | $2$ |\n\nWe now substitute and evaluate as follows:\n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\n\t\\int_{e}^{e^2} \\dfrac{\\ln^2 x}{x}\\,\\textrm{d}x\n&= \\int_{e}^{e^2} (\\ln x)^2\\cdot \\dfrac{\\textrm{d}x}{x}\\[5pt]\n&=\\int_{1}^{2} u^2\\,\\textrm{d}u\\[5pt]\n&=\\left.\\dfrac13u^{3}\\right|_{1}^{2}\\[5pt] \n&=\\dfrac{1}{3}\\left(2^3-1^3 \\right)\\[5pt]\n&=\\dfrac{1}{3}\\left(8-1 \\right)\\[5pt]\n&=\\dfrac{7}{3}\t\t\n\n\t}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186302152 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "fa28f5c4-135e-576a-baa0-68c41b5139f6" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating Functions Containing Other Logarithms"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "10c430ce-b4c9-5ad6-92d3-a2313924c0a1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡6}{3}\\cdot {log}_{6}^{3}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186302154} {:answer/id #uuid "0f3984ae-c6b2-5233-9ae5-32d45bf4dadb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{log}_{6}^{3}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186302155} {:answer/id #uuid "e33122d2-74e0-56a2-8a6b-f7eaa2f44046" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\operatorname{ln}⁡6\\cdot {log}_{6}^{3}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186302156} {:answer/id #uuid "895c6afb-61b9-5702-8402-056efbb6b7e0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}⁡6\\cdot {log}_{6}^{3}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186302157} {:answer/id #uuid "3b971759-66f9-5d4a-83c2-d33e420c3e05" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}⁡6\\cdot {log}_{6}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186302158}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "895c6afb-61b9-5702-8402-056efbb6b7e0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}⁡6\\cdot {log}_{6}^{3}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186302157} :answer-field/id #uuid "0e9fde92-799f-54cb-a163-c8b63400aebb" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186302153}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "06296c2e-56ff-57f8-948e-fc4b28498e50" :question/math-academy-id "q-114020" :question/problem "$\\int \\frac{3{log}_{6}^{2}⁡x}{x}\\,\\text{d}x=$" :question/worked-solution "Let $u={log}_{6}⁡x.$ Differentiating, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡6}\\,⟹\\,\\operatorname{ln}⁡6\\,\\text{d}u=\\frac{\\text{d}x}{x}.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{3{log}_{6}^{2}⁡x}{x}\\,\\text{d}x & =3\\int ({log}_{6}⁡x)^{2}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}x}{x} \\\\  & =3\\int {u}^{2}\\cdot \\operatorname{ln}⁡6\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =3\\operatorname{ln}⁡6\\int {u}^{2}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =3\\operatorname{ln}⁡6\\cdot \\frac{{u}^{3}}{3}+C \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡6\\cdot {log}_{6}^{3}⁡x+C\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186288889 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "41b7d83f-3b9b-556c-9e49-13df9c3b597e" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating Functions Containing the Natural Logarithm"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a56840dc-5e00-5f49-b590-1f3863c348f0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}{ln}^{2}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288891} {:answer/id #uuid "a0dedd3f-bd40-52de-9650-d627896afc09" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{ln}^{2}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288892} {:answer/id #uuid "889ad441-d1c4-56a6-b705-7aa5a5f2f558" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}{ln}^{2}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288893} {:answer/id #uuid "6a605c5d-653a-5ed3-ad3c-426e45c63748" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288894} {:answer/id #uuid "cc76caca-bc0f-52ed-8254-97e818f1b12a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288895}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "889ad441-d1c4-56a6-b705-7aa5a5f2f558" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}{ln}^{2}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288893} :answer-field/id #uuid "291f4bbb-6be7-5dcb-b262-66285993d76d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288890}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "a2a8959c-6b04-5ef7-8052-da57da0ea3d3" :question/math-academy-id "q-13803" :question/problem "Calculate the integral $\\int \\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{2x}\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "Let's set $u=\\operatorname{ln}⁡x.$ Then, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{x}\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}u=\\frac{1}{x}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{2x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{1}{2}\\int \\operatorname{ln}⁡x\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}x}{x} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\int u\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot \\frac{{u}^{2}}{2}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}{u}^{2}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}{ln}^{2}⁡x+C\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186288896 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "41b7d83f-3b9b-556c-9e49-13df9c3b597e" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating Functions Containing the Natural Logarithm"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "190c27db-dd0f-559a-902b-5dbc83d859ee" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{12}{ln}^{2}⁡({x}^{2})+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288898} {:answer/id #uuid "e1ac7ac3-d198-554a-9743-ea0f4f9b7c34" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}{ln}^{2}⁡({x}^{2})+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288899} {:answer/id #uuid "c9f8db47-fddc-5cd3-b5b6-2928fd2958fb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{12}\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2})+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288900} {:answer/id #uuid "473cdab0-4256-5c6c-a43c-0f4779694bf7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{12}{ln}^{2}⁡|x|+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288901} {:answer/id #uuid "fd704b15-f081-5cf0-858c-24b42eb59cc8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{6}{ln}^{2}⁡({x}^{2})+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288902}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "190c27db-dd0f-559a-902b-5dbc83d859ee" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{12}{ln}^{2}⁡({x}^{2})+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288898} :answer-field/id #uuid "84906a4b-b873-5500-8bf5-b8c633338e14" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288897}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "4234ecef-6101-5408-8e19-a789f906baa2" :question/math-academy-id "q-13807" :question/problem "Calculate the integral $\\int \\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2})}{3x}\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "Let's set $u=\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2}).$ Then, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}\\cdot 2x=\\frac{2}{x}\\,⟹\\,\\frac{1}{2}\\text{d}u=\\frac{\\text{d}x}{x}.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2})}{3x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{1}{3}\\int \\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2})\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}x}{x}\\cdot  \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\int u\\cdot (\\frac{1}{2}\\text{d}u) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}\\int u\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}\\cdot \\frac{{u}^{2}}{2}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{12}{u}^{2}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{12}{ln}^{2}⁡({x}^{2})+C\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186318296 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "41b7d83f-3b9b-556c-9e49-13df9c3b597e" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating Functions Containing the Natural Logarithm"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a428892f-9786-5354-8902-0b04d1f32ecb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2})|+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186318298} {:answer/id #uuid "af0abcf0-03ba-5025-8b1b-79060d302527" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5\\operatorname{ln}⁡|\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2})|+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186318299} {:answer/id #uuid "73d79e32-6ad3-58a8-b0bd-b90e310ad78a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}x\\operatorname{ln}⁡|\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2})|+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186318300} {:answer/id #uuid "e9f34528-6233-507a-b4ce-eed1c3f754f2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{2}x\\operatorname{ln}⁡|\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2})|+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186318301} {:answer/id #uuid "3df3201b-ecd7-52dd-9a25-0a78c2a316dd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2})|+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186318302}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3df3201b-ecd7-52dd-9a25-0a78c2a316dd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2})|+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186318302} :answer-field/id #uuid "557bc5c1-c3e8-5ca5-8c71-d36deef5e8f3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186318297}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "7095d0e3-f94b-57ed-bb1d-1a0c31d209b6" :question/math-academy-id "q-13808" :question/problem "Calculate the integral $\\int \\frac{5}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2})}\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "Let's set $u=\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2}).$ Then, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}\\cdot 2x=\\frac{2}{x}\\,⟹\\,\\frac{1}{2}\\text{d}u=\\frac{\\text{d}x}{x}.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{5}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2})}\\,\\text{d}x & =5\\int \\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2})}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}x}{x} \\\\  & =5\\int \\frac{1}{u}\\cdot (\\frac{1}{2}\\text{d}u) \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{2}\\int \\frac{1}{u}\\cdot \\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|u|+C \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2})|+C\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186302173 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "41b7d83f-3b9b-556c-9e49-13df9c3b597e" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating Functions Containing the Natural Logarithm"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5d2b2e3d-82cd-5211-9fd1-82df01b15fb8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}⁡|\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2x)|+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186302175} {:answer/id #uuid "c4ed3294-f23b-5a37-812b-3200429d67a0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|\\operatorname{ln}⁡(4x)|+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186302176} {:answer/id #uuid "a4ea221c-eb86-54f2-975b-1fe1e977f711" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4\\operatorname{ln}⁡|\\operatorname{ln}⁡x|+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186302177} {:answer/id #uuid "8cea49ee-13f7-504a-a8de-361c53d4a306" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2x)|+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186302178} {:answer/id #uuid "b190b52b-d15a-56a3-8ef9-330d4f32c85f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|\\operatorname{ln}⁡(4x)|+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186302179}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c4ed3294-f23b-5a37-812b-3200429d67a0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|\\operatorname{ln}⁡(4x)|+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186302176} :answer-field/id #uuid "723f76f6-078b-5048-9166-e625436b5904" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186302174}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "640d756b-d216-53d7-813b-ffeca4e75575" :question/math-academy-id "q-210746" :question/problem "Calculate the integral $\\int \\frac{2}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡(4x)}\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "Let's set $u=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(4x).$ Then, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{4x}\\cdot 4\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}u=\\frac{1}{x}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{2}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡(4x)}\\,\\text{d}x & =2\\int \\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(4x)}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}x}{x} \\\\  & =2\\int \\frac{1}{u}\\cdot \\text{d}u \\\\  & =2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|u|+C \\\\  & =2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|\\operatorname{ln}⁡(4x)|+C\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186318303 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "41b7d83f-3b9b-556c-9e49-13df9c3b597e" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating Functions Containing the Natural Logarithm"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "03f48953-f2f7-5f8d-8f8f-1a67b5d2524d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{x}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186318305} {:answer/id #uuid "28adc6c8-aa2f-50db-9fb5-d12735aaf371" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)}}{x}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186318306} {:answer/id #uuid "d2a72e29-8f50-5d0d-83b2-3322ade7ee10" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186318307} {:answer/id #uuid "6fe125c4-ccae-54bf-89e3-b2e2937a717a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186318308} {:answer/id #uuid "d294cfa1-d1f9-5f18-aa18-8c7c6f0ab21c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\sqrt{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186318309}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d294cfa1-d1f9-5f18-aa18-8c7c6f0ab21c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\sqrt{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186318309} :answer-field/id #uuid "3003d995-ec63-5573-a343-1b41701124da" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186318304}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "14d64831-00ec-512c-8691-072b09db6f00" :question/math-academy-id "q-2380" :question/problem "Calculate the integral $\\int \\frac{1}{x\\sqrt{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}}\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "Let's set $u=\\operatorname{ln}⁡x.$ Then, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{x}\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}u=\\frac{\\text{d}x}{x}.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{1}{x\\sqrt{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}x}{x} \\\\  & =\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{u}}\\cdot \\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\int {u}^{-1/2}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =2{u}^{1/2}+C \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186101287 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "fa28f5c4-135e-576a-baa0-68c41b5139f6" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating Functions Containing Other Logarithms"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "81c36c65-35ca-5d52-a03d-92482fb6b1cb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\ln 2 \\cdot \\frac{\\log_{2} x}{2} + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186099339} {:answer/id #uuid "ef822792-3cf4-5a17-86ee-bb3dbb4f35a6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\ln x \\cdot \\frac{\\log_{2}^{2} x}{2} + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186099340} {:answer/id #uuid "f225c7a5-c416-5406-a430-71fcc48bcc5a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\ln 2 \\cdot \\frac{\\log_{2}^{2} x}{2} + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186099341} {:answer/id #uuid "127c18f7-2532-52ea-bf09-7ea32a936b5e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\ln x \\cdot \\frac{\\log_{2}^{2} x}{x} + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186099342} {:answer/id #uuid "399c3e46-e63f-548b-ad88-0cb54e0a6e39" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\ln 3 \\cdot \\frac{\\log_{2} x}{2} + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186099343}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f225c7a5-c416-5406-a430-71fcc48bcc5a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\ln 2 \\cdot \\frac{\\log_{2}^{2} x}{2} + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186099341} :answer-field/id #uuid "4456b3bc-a2cb-5663-9041-ec22b84552ac" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186099338}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "bc1950d7-cc9c-5e9a-8f86-5dcc05de2e91" :question/math-academy-id "q-31329" :question/problem "$\\int \\frac{{log}_{2}⁡x}{x}\\,\\text{d}x=$" :question/worked-solution "Let $u={log}_{2}⁡x.$ Differentiating, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}\\,⟹\\,\\operatorname{ln}⁡2\\,\\text{d}u=\\frac{\\text{d}x}{x}.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{{log}_{2}⁡x}{x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int {log}_{2}⁡x\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}x}{x} \\\\  & =\\int u\\cdot \\operatorname{ln}⁡2\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡2\\int u\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡2\\cdot \\frac{{u}^{2}}{2}+C \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡2\\cdot \\frac{{log}_{2}^{2}⁡x}{2}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186318310 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "fa28f5c4-135e-576a-baa0-68c41b5139f6" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating Functions Containing Other Logarithms"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "84ca7593-d513-5f3b-846f-5f5bb10b6d00" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}⁡x\\cdot \\frac{{log}_{5}^{2}⁡x}{x}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186318312} {:answer/id #uuid "079369c5-5eb2-59b2-9d81-e29b505cd774" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}⁡5\\cdot \\frac{{log}_{5}^{2}⁡x}{2}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186318313} {:answer/id #uuid "6d8c2a10-f81e-563d-ab01-15d6bffaca93" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}⁡5\\cdot \\frac{{log}_{3}⁡x}{2}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186318314} {:answer/id #uuid "a0dc4a3